Text:
  These are algebraic ingredients for perturbation-indexed well groups.
  The ambient space and scalar structure are fixed explicitly.
  This file does not assert the two-extreme-perturbation characterization.

Context indexed subspaces:
  Let K,V,I: Type
  Let f: FieldStructure(K)
  Let L: LinearSpace(K,f,V)
  Let A: Set(I)
  Let S: Function(I,Subspace(K,f,V,L))

  Result indexed intersection membership:
    Attribution: mathlib; Submodule.mem_sInf; adapted
    Let x: V
    Conclude:
      belongs to subspace(f,L,x,intersection of subspaces(f,L,A,S)) ↔
        for every (i: I, i ∈ A → belongs to subspace(f,L,x,S(i)))

  Result intersection is included in each member:
    Attribution: mathlib; Submodule.mem_sInf; adapted
    Let i: I
    Assume admissible index: i ∈ A
    Conclude:
      subspace included in(f,L,intersection of subspaces(f,L,A,S),S(i))

  Result more indices give a smaller intersection:
    Attribution: mathlib; Submodule.mem_sInf; adapted
    Let B: Set(I)
    Assume more indices: A ⊆ B
    Conclude:
      subspace included in(f,L,
        intersection of subspaces(f,L,B,S),
        intersection of subspaces(f,L,A,S))

  Result empty family contains every vector:
    Attribution: mathlib; Submodule.mem_sInf; adapted
    Let x: V
    Assume no admissible indices: for every (i: I, not i ∈ A)
    Conclude:
      belongs to subspace(f,L,x,intersection of subspaces(f,L,A,S))

